From fc5e8e2b020bbab893cca94afdd38df3ce47eda0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 10:00:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02324/11362] [outer-loop] ARC heuristic SELECTION learning:
 when (and when not) to use which

Answers the operator audit: 'have we learned WHEN to use these heuristics; is
the learning phase updated; are heuristics missing?' Honest gap found: the
heuristics were captured per-game but NOT wired into the solve loop, and there
was NO encoded selection rule. Fixed all three:

1. WHEN-to-use-which is now learned + encoded (arc_heuristic_select):
   - feature = per-action CELL IMPACT (median cells changed/move, from transitions)
   - rule (recommend_order): no win-state -> BFS (a goal heuristic needs a target);
     cell-impact >=~40 -> region_count first; <40 -> cell_count first; BFS last.
   - validated: su15 (impact 20) -> chose cell_count (1406); r11l (70) -> region_count
     (optimal 3/257); sk48 (74) -> region_count (cell_count FAILS that game).

2. DYNAMIC ADAPTATION to unseen games: select_best() runs the portfolio,
   reproduction-gates, picks by path-optimality then expansions, BANKS the winner.
   bank_for_solved_game() (1 search, cheap) is wired into the standing loop
   (arc_loop_solve.solve_via_explore) GUARDED so every fresh solve learns + captures
   its best heuristic live -- never breaks the solve. recommend_approach() now
   surfaces heuristic_policy in every new-game recipe (the new-game flow already
   calls it). Selection rule recorded in ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml (auditable;
   includes HOW to extend with a new heuristic).

3. MISSING heuristic classes logged (ops/verifier_gaps.md): deep-sparse (wa30-class,
   region-count is flat early -> no gradient), object-displacement/manhattan (for
   move-a-piece-to-target games region-count can't see distance), condition/predicate
   distance (condition-win games have no fixed target grid).

Plus cell_count_distance factory + 8 asserting unit tests for the rule/feature/factory.
33 tests pass, no regression.
